Defines standard system pressures (in kilopascals) divided into two distinct engineering sequences:
a) Principal Series: Standard pressures from which pressure values required for the normal operation of equipment are selected;
b) Additional Series: Standard pressures reserved for exceptional or highly specialized cases only.

Classifies side scuttles into three distinct types depending on their installation location:
a) Heavy Type (Type A): Designed for watertight and gastight requirements, installed below the freeboard deck or in the hull below the full load waterline;
b) Medium Type (Type B): Installed above the freeboard deck in the first tier of superstructures (cargo vessels);
c) Light Type (Type C): Installed above the freeboard deck in superstructures for passenger vessels.

Side scuttles must be configured as either:
a) Opening Type: Equipped with a hinged glassholder that can be swung open for ventilation;
b) Non-opening Type: Fixed model where the glassholder is secured permanently to the main frame.

Enforces strict height limits for marking characters (such as nominal size, ply rating, load index) depending on nominal rim diameter:
a) Up to 12 inches: b = 4 mm minimum, c = 4 mm minimum;
b) 13 to 19.5 inches: b = 6 mm minimum, c = 4 mm minimum;
k) 20 inches and above: b = 9 mm minimum, c = 4 mm minimum.

Classifies all light two-wheelers, three-wheelers, and quadricycles:
- L1: Two-wheelers with maximum design speed <= 50 km/h (displacement <= 50 cc for thermal or <= 4 kW for electric engines);
- L2: Three-wheelers with maximum design speed <= 50 km/h (displacement <= 50 cc or <= 4 kW);
- L3: Two-wheeled motorcycles with speed > 50 km/h (displacement > 50 cc);
- L4: Motorcycles with an asymmetrical sidecar, speed > 50 km/h;
- L5: Symmetrically arranged three-wheelers (auto-rickshaws), speed > 50 km/h. Subdivided into L5-M (Passenger Carrier) and L5-N (Goods Carrier);
- L6: Light quadricycles with unladen mass <= 350 kg, speed <= 45 km/h, max power <= 4 kW;
- L7: Heavy quadricycles with unladen mass <= 400 kg (or <= 550 kg for goods transport), max speed <= 45 km/h, max continuous power <= 15 kW.

Classifies all four-wheeled motor vehicles designed and constructed for carrying passengers:
- M1: Vehicles comprising not more than 8 seats in addition to the driver's seat (passenger cars);
- M2: Vehicles comprising 9 or more seats in addition to the driver's seat, with a Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW) not exceeding 5 tonnes;
- M3: Vehicles comprising 9 or more seats in addition to the driver's seat, with a Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW) exceeding 5 tonnes (commercial buses).

Classifies all four-wheeled motor vehicles designed and constructed for carrying goods:
- N1: Vehicles used for the carriage of goods, having a Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW) not exceeding 3.5 tonnes;
- N2: Vehicles used for the carriage of goods, having a Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW) exceeding 3.5 tonnes but not exceeding 12 tonnes;
- N3: Vehicles used for the carriage of goods, having a Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW) exceeding 12 tonnes.

Under India-specific CMVR and AIS alignment, towed trailers are designated as Category T (as opposed to Category O internationally):
- T1: Trailers and semi-trailers having a maximum weight not exceeding 0.75 tonnes;
- T2: Trailers and semi-trailers having a maximum weight exceeding 0.75 tonnes but not exceeding 3.5 tonnes;
- T3: Trailers and semi-trailers having a maximum weight exceeding 3.5 tonnes but not exceeding 10 tonnes;
- T4: Trailers and semi-trailers having a maximum weight exceeding 10 tonnes;
- T5: Semi-trailers intended to be drawn by a three-wheeled haulage tractor.

Classifies pneumatic tyres into two distinct categories depending on service severity:
a) Type A — Heavy duty tyres (specifically recommended for load-carrying cycle rickshaws);
b) Type B — Standard duty tyres (recommended for conventional passenger cycles / bicycles).

Tyres are specified based on edge style to match various wheel rim profiles:
a) Wired Edge: Tyres mounted on straight side/wired-on rims;
b) Beaded Edge: Tyres mounted on hooked bead rims.

The structural casing cords must be manufactured from either:
a) Grey cotton yarn conforming to IS 7133;
b) Polyamide yarn/Nylon fabric conforming to IS 11573.

The welded joints of the steel bead wire must satisfy strict minimum ultimate breaking loads:
a) Type B (Standard Duty): Cotton Tyres require >= 128 kgf (1260 N); Nylon Tyres require >= 200 kgf (1960 N);
b) Type A (Heavy Duty): Cotton Tyres require >= 229 kgf (2250 N); Nylon Tyres require >= 400 kgf (3920 N).

Tyres must undergo continuous drum testing at a speed of 24 km/h under three progressive loading stages (Stage I, II, and III) at specified inflation pressures. For example:
a) Size 32-630 (at 480 kPa): Stage I = 72 kg, Stage II = 78 kg, Stage III = 84 kg;
b) Size 40-635 Type A (at 410 kPa): Stage I = 103 kg, Stage II = 111 kg, Stage III = 120 kg;
c) Size 40-635 Type B (at 410 kPa): Stage I = 86 kg, Stage II = 93 kg, Stage III = 100 kg.

To guide bicycle manufacturers in designing proper wheel fork and mudguard clearance envelopes, maximum service dimensions are calculated as:
a) Max Width: W_max = S + 3 mm (where S is design new section width);
b) Max Diameter: D_max = Dr + 2H + 6 mm (where Dr is nominal rim diameter and H is section height).

Under Part 3 Amendment 1, the maximum sound levels for three-wheelers are:
a) Vehicles with engine capacity <= 175 cc (thermic) or battery-operated vehicles (including E-rickshaws, E-carts): 76 dB(A);
b) Vehicles with engine capacity > 175 cc (thermic): 80 dB(A).

Maximum sound limits for L2 category motorcycles are:
a) Engine displacement <= 80 cc: 75 dB(A);
b) 80 cc < Displacement <= 175 cc: 77 dB(A);
c) Displacement > 175 cc: 80 dB(A).

Table 1 defines the nominal size ranges (400 mm to 1600 mm) along with the dimensions D1, D2, pitch diameters, number of teeth, and sections of the wheel. Examples:
a) Size 400: D1 = 427 mm, D2 = 510 mm, Pitch Dia = 561.8 mm, No. of Teeth = 42, Wheel Sections = 2;
b) Size 800: D1 = 828 mm, D2 = 912 mm, Pitch Dia = 963.1 mm, No. of Teeth = 72, Wheel Sections = 4;
c) Size 1600: D1 = 1630 mm, D2 = 1713 mm, Pitch Dia = 1791.5 mm, No. of Teeth = 134, Wheel Sections = 6.

The number of guide rollers used around the circumference of the coaming varies strictly by ventilator nominal size:
a) Nominal sizes 400 to 700 mm: Requires 3 rollers;
b) Nominal sizes 800 to 1100 mm: Requires 4 rollers;
c) Nominal sizes 1250 to 1600 mm: Requires 6 rollers.

The spherically seated washer used inside the pivot bearing must comply with standard sizing codes:
a) For Nominal Sizes 400 to 1250 mm: Use T 80.80.10 washer;
b) For Nominal Sizes 1400 and 1600 mm: Use T 100.100.10 washer.

Defines three structural thickness categories depending on pressure/location:
a) Category 1 (Standard): up to 300 mm is 1 mm GI sheet; 300 to 500 mm is 1.5 mm GI; over 500 mm is 2 mm GI;
b) Category 2: up to 500 mm is 2 mm GI; 500 to 750 mm is 3 mm MS; over 750 mm is 4 mm MS;
c) Category 3 (Engine Room/Heavy plate): Any size is 4 to 8 mm MS depending on location.

Establishes standard materials for all block components: 
a) Cheeks: Grey Cast Iron (IS 210 Gr 25), Spheroidal Graphite Iron (IS 1865 Gr SG 38), Whiteheart (IS 2107) or Blackheart (IS 2108) Malleable Iron, C20 wrought carbon steel (IS 1570), or Cast Steel (IS 1030);
b) Sheave: Siemens Martin wrought steel C20 or fully killed open-hearth steel C15 (IS 1570);
c) Axle Pin, Locking Plate, and Hinged Straps (Main & Locking Pieces): fully killed open-hearth steel C15;
d) Pin for Hinged supporting strap: wrought carbon steel C30;
e) Supporting Cross-Head: wrought steel C15 or Cast Steel (IS 1030);
f) Oval Eye, Head Fitting, and Round Nuts: wrought carbon steel C20.

Specifies detailed cheek dimensions (in mm) for nominal sizes 150 to 400. Examples:
a) Size 150: h1 = 150 mm, h2 = 50 mm, d2 = 25 mm, h3 = 166 mm, h4 = 71 mm, d3 = 35 mm, l5 = 55 mm, s1 = 3 mm, t5 = 26 mm, b2 = 50 mm, b3 = 24 mm;
b) Size 400: h1 = 400 mm, h2 = 130 mm, d2 = 70 mm, h3 = 445 mm, h4 = 189 mm, d3 = 90 mm, l5 = 145 mm, s1 = 7 mm, t5 = 78 mm, b2 = 130 mm, b3 = 62 mm.

Specifies strict dimensional limits across nominal shank diameters (1.6 to 9.6 mm) for five key head parameters:
a) Head Diameter (D): ranges from 3.2 ±0.15 mm (for d=1.6) to 19.0 ±0.9 mm (for d=9.6);
b) Head Height (E): ranges from 0.7 mm (for d=1.6) to 4.1 mm (for d=9.6);
c) Head Side Flat (F): ranges from 0.4 mm (for d=1.6) to 2.4 mm (for d=9.6);
d) Crown Radius (G): ranges from 1.4 mm (for d=1.6) to 8.3 mm (for d=9.6);
e) Edge Radius r (Reference only): ranges from 0.15 mm to 0.25 mm.

To prevent metallurgical mix-ups on the assembly floor, rivets must be physically marked on the head or on the end of the shank with indented symbols:
a) Alloy No. 1: Two indented circular dots (maximum diameter of 0.8 mm);
b) Alloy No. 2: Two indented circular dots with a curved line or dash.

Establishes a strict colour coding system mapped against specific colour reference numbers from IS 5 : 1978 for 8 different shipboard ventilation circuits:
1. Natural Supply Air: Yellow (Colour Reference No. 309);
2. Natural Exhaust Air: Brown (Colour Reference No. 489);
3. Mechanical Supply Air (atmospheric fresh air): Green (Colour Reference No. 218);
4. Mechanical Supply Air, warm (heated air): Pink (Colour Reference No. 443);
5. Mechanical Supply Air, cold (refrigerated air): Dark Blue (Colour Reference No. 166);
6. Conditioned Supply Air: Violet (Colour Reference No. 796);
7. Mechanical Recirculated Air (return air): Orange (Colour Reference No. 592);
8. Mechanical Exhaust Air: Grey (Colour Reference No. 694).
